*.before*
*.before_sed
*.tmp
cinemagoer.db
app.js.bak3

# Player layout harness fixture (downloaded by frontend/harness/README.md, not source)
frontend/public/harness-sample.mp4

# ---- Apple clients (apple/) ----
# Xcode per-user state must never be committed; everything else in the projects IS source.
**/xcuserdata/
**/*.xcuserstate
**/*.xcscmblueprint
**/DerivedData/
**/.build/
**/.swiftpm/configuration/
**/*.moved-aside
**/Pods/

# The Xcode projects are created ONCE in Xcode and COMMITTED (apple/WORKFLOW.md §2). Only
# Xcode writes a valid .xcodeproj, and the sources live inside the synchronized folder it
# owns, so the project IS source here, not build output. Per-user state stays ignored.
# ⚠ If we ever move to XcodeGen (§2.1) this flips: ignore the generated *.xcodeproj and
# commit project.yml instead.
apple/**/*.xcworkspace/

# Test-run logs. They travel back by PASTING (apple/LOGGING.md §7); if a whole file ever
# needs to reach the repo, un-ignore that one file explicitly: git add -f apple/logs/<file>
apple/logs/

# Generated API types ARE committed on purpose (see apple/scripts/generate-api.sh) —
# do not ignore apple/**/Core/GeneratedAPI/.

# Debug screenshots. ⚠ Added 2026-09-19 the hard way: a 268 KB device screenshot was swept into a commit
# by `git add -A`, and this repo does not want binary evidence in its history. Screenshots travel the same
# way logs do — they are pasted/attached, and the file stays on the desk.
debug_screenshots/
*.heic
